{"model":"qwen2.5:3b","created_at":"2026-10-28T13:26:31.983197414Z","response":"```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import qmc\n\ndef pack_circles(n: int) -\u003e np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pack n circles in a unit square to maximize sum of radii using Sobol sequence for initialization and simulated annealing with Gaussian perturbations.\n\n    Args:\n        n: Number of circles to pack\n\n    Returns:\n        Numpy array of shape (n, 3) where each row is (x, y, radius)\n        All values should be between 0 and 1\n        Circles must not overlap\n        \n    Important: Set \"all\" random seeds to 2025, including the packages (such as scipy sub-packages) involving random seeds.\n    \"\"\"\n    np.random.seed(2025)\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.zeros((0, 3))\n    \n    # Sobol sequence initialization\n    sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, seed=2025)\n    points = sampler.random(n)\n    circles = np.zeros((n, 3))\n    circles[:, :2] = points\n    \n    # Simulated annealing with Gaussian perturbations and exponential cooling\n    for iteration in range(4000):\n        temperature = 0.9 * (iteration / 1000) + 0.1\n        \n        for i in range(n):\n            x, y, r = circles[i]\n            \n            # Radius expansion\n            max_r = min(x, 1-x, y, 1-y)\n            for j in range(n):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                dist = np.sqrt((circles[j,0]-x)**2 + (circles[j,1]-y)**2)\n                max_r = min(max_r, dist - circles[j,2])\n            \n            # Gaussian perturbations\n            for _ in range(3):\n                step_size = 0.05 * np.random.randn()\n                new_x = x + step_size if np.random.rand() \u003c 0.5 else x - step_size\n                new_y = y + step_size if np.random.rand() \u003c 0.5 else y - step_size\n                \n                current_r = min(new_x, 1-new_x, new_y, 1-new_y)\n                for j in range(n):\n                    if i == j:\n                        continue\n                    dist = np.sqrt((circles[j,0]-new_x)**2 + (circles[j,1]-new_y)**2)\n                    current_r = min(current_r, dist - circles[j,2])\n                \n                if current_r \u003e r and np.random.rand() \u003c np.exp((current_r - r) / temperature):\n                    circles[i] = [new_x, new_y, current_r]\n    \n    # Ensure all circles are within the unit square\n    for i in range(n):\n        x, y, _ = circles[i]\n        if not (0 \u003c= x \u003c= 1 and 0 \u003c= y \u003c= 1):\n            circles[i] = np.random.rand(3) * 2 - 1\n    \n    # Ensure pairwise non-overlap\n    def overlap(c1, c2):\n        return np.sqrt((c1[0]-c2[0])**2 + (c1[1]-c2[1])**2) \u003c c1[2] + c2[2]\n    \n    while any(overlap(circles[i], circles[j]) for i in range(n) for j in range(i+1, n)):\n        for i in range(n):\n            x, y, r = circles[i]\n            min_overlap_x = max(x - r, 0)\n            max_overlap_x = min(x + r, 1)\n            min_overlap_y = max(y - r, 0)\n            max_overlap_y = min(y + r, 1)\n            \n            for j in range(n):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                cx, cy, cr = circles[j]\n                \n                # Check if there is an overlap and adjust the position of circle i\n                if (min_overlap_x \u003c= cx \u003c max_overlap_x and min_overlap_y \u003c= cy \u003c max_overlap_y) or \\\n                   (min_overlap_y \u003c= cx \u003c max_overlap_y and min_overlap_x \u003c= cy \u003c max_overlap_x):\n                    dx = x - cx\n                    dy = y - cy\n                    \n                    # Calculate the new position for circle i after perturbation\n                    if np.random.rand() \u003c 0.5:\n                        x_new = x + (cx - x) * np.random.randn()\n                    else:\n                        x_new = x - (x - cx) * np.random.randn()\n                    \n                    if np.random.rand() \u003c 0.5:\n                        y_new = y + (cy - y) * np.random.randn()\n                    else:\n                        y_new = y - (y - cy) * np.random.randn()\n                    \n                    # Ensure the new position is within bounds\n                    x_new = max(0, min(x_new, 1))\n                    y_new = max(0, min(y_new, 1))\n                    \n                    circles[i] = [x_new, y_new, r]\n    \n    return circles\n```\n\nThis program introduces a simulated annealing approach with Gaussian perturbations for initializing the circle positions and adjusting them to maximize the sum of radii while ensuring all circles fit within the unit square without overlapping. The cooling schedule is adjusted from exponential to linear, and the search space is explored using Gaussian noise instead of Cauchy noise.","done":true,"done_reason":"stop","context":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,31115,264,501,25262,12111,369,35713,220,17,21,25362,315,10767,2155,11900,72,304,279,4982,9334,13,7487,11853,279,2629,315,11900,72,26,3412,2169,374,518,3245,220,17,13,21,18,21,15,13,1096,2169,374,537,19323,624,5598,6896,825,13027,2038,2504,8482,264,4583,2025,448,6896,825,1909,11591,729,3769,666,74263,1445,25,526,8,1464,2595,35549,13,51075,15202,25,8591,11,6888,11,28090,13,3155,537,2924,1909,11591,11320,11,10295,11,13137,5746,476,60701,4889,279,2038,2504,13,3411,264,34226,320,77,11,220,18,8,1334,315,320,87,7358,15883,701,2477,42224,11900,72,11,45211,323,678,2268,4720,2477,28252,15958,13,5443,72349,4194,19056,8356,311,220,17,15,17,20,323,61115,34447,13,576,3412,69810,5711,308,28,17,21,323,264,220,17,15,43863,24203,11320,3930,13,1096,374,264,3412,3930,11,537,264,11660,3946,8645,5912,624,785,17221,13656,2025,374,458,93947,2884,5785,11,537,264,5023,16548,50282,13,11445,9768,5456,1231,2525,504,264,2155,4573,476,15592,8039,13,81306,279,3749,11,714,6923,697,1828,32156,